notes=[
('The learner actually traces a finite plant/animal key and preserves missing-observation limits. Plant P1 heart-shaped and unlobed already uniquely selects B among the supplied four candidates: the task demand that shape alone is insufficient has a false premise.','P3 only unlobed leaves B/D possible; T3 six legs supports an insect group, with an explicit request for wing evidence. These transfers distinguish a data gap from invented identification.','One identification procedure, applied to different organism types and incomplete observations.','An external key supplies names and distinguishing traits; reliable reasoning through a key is the competence, not a new species-name recall deck.'),
('Flight ecology and ancestry classifications answer different questions; bat/mouse hair and mammary homologies differ from bat/bird convergent flight.','The O000/A100/B110/C111 matrix supports B/C via m2 and ABC via m1 under stated assumptions; conflicting A/C markers demand homology/convergence and alternate-tree review.','One critical classification comparison; evaluate is the consequence of compare.','Traits and matrix are supplied; classification logic and evidence quality cannot be replaced by isolated memorized labels.'),
('Pre-exposure colony variation and later selection are separated from need-directed mutation; stress increasing mutation rates is not adaptive targeting.','The plant common-condition offspring contrast distinguishes plasticity from inherited regulatory variation; one-generation epigenetic persistence does not prove universal inheritance of acquired traits.','One test of compatibility between an evolutionary explanation and genetics.','The two explanations are assessed with evidence; no indispensable new compact recall item is established by this goal.'),
('The founder shift 0.4 to0.7 is drift before drought selection; mutation/recombination, environmental selection and reduced gene flow contribute distinct causal links.','Same-area host timing can restrict reproduction despite laboratory fertility; removing a barrier changes predictions rather than automatically creating or ending a species.','One explanatory use of the synthetic theory to account for diversification and speciation.','Material supplies observations and frequencies; causal mechanism distinctions are understanding, not a required deck.'),
('The primate founder/diet/mating model applies ordinary synthetic mechanisms without a human-value hierarchy or inevitable progress.','Equal-contribution migration gives0.32; sterile migrants contribute no gene flow. Fertile offspring/partial mating barriers do not warrant a complete species claim.','One application of the synthetic theory, including a primate context.','The hypothetical data and conditions are supplied; this goal does not require a separate primate-name or allele-frequency recall deck.'),
('Food processing transmission18/20 versus4/20 supports efficient cultural teaching; horizontal/vertical language-mediated knowledge is distinguished from allele transmission.','Shelter8 versus14 units of fuel illustrates contingent environmental benefit; toxin misinformation or hot-habitat overheating defeats an automatic cultural-progress/fitness claim.','One explanation of how cultural transmission can affect adaptation and spread.','Reason about conditional cultural effects; figures and procedure examples are supplied rather than hard facts to recall.'),
('Irrigation changes habitat conditions immediately, whereas selection changes inherited-variant frequencies through differential reproduction across generations; water/salt and other habitat risks are retained.','Breeding0.4 to0.9 narrows the pool conditionally; seed banking is not guaranteed resistance. Descriptive biology supplies no normative ranking of human worth.','One mechanism comparison with assessment of the consequences of human intervention.','The competence is comparison and risk evaluation; no mandatory isolated memory item or memory-node trace is established.'),
('Kin model rB-C=.5 becomes-1 for unrelated recipients and-.5 for B1; the counterfactual increment and excluded other benefits are stated.','Current/future offspring5 versus6 changes to7 versus6 in the wet context; offspring counts and survival alone are not measured lifetime inclusive fitness.','One inclusive-fitness analysis with direct and indirect reproductive components.','The simple expression and numbers are supplied; interpreting the model and its limits is primary, not automatic formula memorization.'),
('GA learners make their own time-budget/cost table: both10min, A net6.5, B net3. Active cooperation is operationally distinct from proximity; short synthetic observations are not real fieldwork or demonstrated reproduction.','Optimal foraging X2/Y5 reverses toX7 when risk changes; threat proportions and care patterns are conditional/confounded rather than reproductive proof.','One application of behavioral-ecology methods across cooperation/aggression/reproduction, not independent new organism-fact lists.','Ethogram/cost definitions are supplied. Method choice, coding and inference need practice and critique rather than a required memory deck.'),
('EA adds sender/signal/receiver/response. A net5/B1.5 and80% versus20% response document association while danger/rank confounds prevent causal certainty.','Own eight-event classification distinguishes3truewarnings/2falsealarms/1miss/2trueabsence; receiver response and energetic measures do not directly establish inclusive fitness or intent.','One behavioral-ecology inquiry method extended to communication as expressly required at EA.','The supplied ethogram and response criteria support analytic performance; no compact recall deck is necessary to this goal.'),
('Scarce8/20 versus rich3/20 threats and hormones admit proximate exogenous/endogenous explanations with age/rank confounds; school-rule examples require cultural context.','Primate/human care comparisons distinguish ultimate hypotheses from proximate mechanisms and normative gender roles; unrelated help tests exclusive kin-selection explanations.','One critical multi-causal application of primate social behavior to human behavior.','The goal calls for causal discrimination and critical transfer, not fixed social-behavior stereotypes or fact recall.'),
('The4600my scale puts0.30my Homo sapiens at0.00652cm on100cm, matching0.0652mm; the600my inset gives0.5mm. The species is recent without becoming a purposeful endpoint.','The24h Earth model places the endpoint about5.63s before midnight;23:00 would correspond to roughly191.7my. Scale changes do not change elapsed historical time.','One temporal placement of modern humans within evolutionary history.','The approximate dates are supplied for scale reasoning; a new chronology deck is not forced by a placement goal.'),
('Anatomy plus the explicitly synthetic20-position sequence comparison supports nested chordate/mammal/primate/great-ape placement, not descent from a living chimpanzee or a real whole-genome distance.','Human/ostrich bipedality can converge; changed locomotor ability in a person does not change taxonomy. Discordant loci require wider evidence rather than canceling all homologies.','One evidence-based systematic placement using anatomical and molecular data.','Class labels are scaffolding in the cases; homology reasoning and evidence limits remain the learning mechanism, no new mandatory recall deck proven.'),
('F1–F4 overlapping dates and traits support bounded fossil hypotheses without a linear ladder; tools in a layer do not prove maker/speech. Savanna absence can reflect sampling/preservation.','Modern agriculture/knowledge affects people and the biosphere without new genetic inheritance. That present-day cultural-impact analysis can be performed independently of the fossil reconstruction, so atomicity warrants developer review.','Uncertain: reconstruct ancient biological evolution from fossils and analyze modern cultural influence are two separately assessable outcomes; shared human-evolution subject matter alone does not prove one routine.','No memory deck is justified by these inferential and evaluative demands, even while atomicity remains uncertain.'),
('Ash bracketing conservatively yields1.7–2.5my; 1:3 parent/daughter gives2half-lives under initial-daughter-zero/closed-system assumptions. However the bilingual claim that C14 requires organic material is overly universal and factually false for suitable terrestrial carbonates.','Reworking breaks the relevant stratigraphic bound; daughter loss biases the age downward. Derived homologous traits and dated fossils support minimum lineage records, not exact ancestors/divergence.','One fossil-evidence interpretation combining dating and constrained lineage inference.','Constants, method premises and data are supplied. Critical dating/phylogenetic interpretation does not require an automatic formula/date deck.'),
('80 residents at0.25 and20 contributing immigrants at0.75 yield70/200 copies=0.35; half immigrant gamete contribution gives0.30556. Movement alone is not gene flow.','Sterile migration changes demography only;10% successful0.9 gametes raises0.1 to0.18. Separate immigrant mating is not demonstrated transfer to the resident breeding population.','One explanation and application of gene flow versus migration.','Own frequency reasoning uses supplied data and explicitly stated contribution conditions; a separate memorization layer is unnecessary.'),
('Ectopic posterior Hox expression changes positional identity in a hypothetical developmental network; unchanged coding sequence does not mean unchanged spatial regulation.','Earlier/longer regulator expression can change morphology if heritable; independent pathways can converge. Warm-rearing plasticity and sterile developmental change do not prove inherited evolutionary divergence or a new species.','One Evo-Devo explanation linking regulated development with the possible origins of inherited morphological diversity.','This goal needs model reasoning and causal distinctions; no required inventory of gene names or developmental dates is established.'),
('The given Lamarck/Darwin/synthetic accounts differ in mechanisms; modern drift explains random loss under the supplied accounts, without claiming Darwin could never discuss unselected change.','Testable conditional predictions differ from teleological final perfection and nonempirical belief. Limited epigenetic evidence does not validate universal acquired inheritance or warrant dismissal of science.','One critical comparison of scientific evolutionary explanations and their explanatory limits.','Accounts are supplied for comparison. Historical labels may aid orientation but do not establish a compulsory SRS deck.')]
